1.9.1 Context - {Findings: Previous exploitation attempts were unsuccessful; however, a new potential exploitation method has been identified.}  
       1.9.2 New Exploit Identified - {Findings: Exploit Name: BadSuccessor; Source: Detailed in a blog post by Akamai (link: [BadSuccessor Exploit](https://www.akamai.com/blog/security-research/abusing-dmsa-for-privilege-escalation-in-active-directory))}  
       1.9.3 Overview of BadSuccessor - {Findings: This exploitation method leverages vulnerabilities within Active Directory to facilitate privilege escalation; it specifically abuses the Domain Management Security Association (DMSA) for unauthorized privilege elevation.}  
       1.9.4 Implications - {Findings: If successfully exploited, BadSuccessor could allow attackers to gain higher privileges within the Active Directory environment, potentially compromising user accounts and administrative roles.}  
       1.9.5 Next Steps - {Findings: Further investigation into the BadSuccessor exploit is warranted to understand its mechanics and potential impact; assess the current Active Directory configurations to identify any vulnerabilities that might be susceptible to this exploit; consider implementing mitigations or patches as recommended by the source to protect against this privilege escalation method.
